    "definition": "A record is in when NID's STATE field (eye's details.state) puts it in Texas and its point lies inside, or within 0.05 degrees of, eye's outline state:48 from https://eye.jcamd.com/api/economy?op=areas&level=state (Census TIGERweb, generalised 1:20M; response sha256 e43aaa9eecb50a923507578c16309b9b8199b158ed84e138bbb419c654ddbaa3, retrieved 2026-10-18T23:06:58.575Z). The tolerance covers the generalised coast and river borders; the source's own state field decides between neighbours. bbox is the widened outline's extent. Records came from 46 requests to eye's infra?op=dams: 1.5-degree boxes on eye's 0.25-degree grid that touch the widened outline, each split in four while eye said truncated (0 split), deduplicated by id."
  },
